WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.640
Relationships describe how many rows can connect
between entities In

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:09.364
a one-to-one relationship each side connects to at
most one row on

00:00:09.391 --> 00:00:14.960
the other side In a one-to-many relationship one
parent can connect

00:00:14.987 --> 00:00:19.463
to many child rows A patient can have many
appointments so the

00:00:19.476 --> 00:00:25.177
foreign key belongs on the appointment side In a
many-to-many relationship

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:30.706
both sides can connect to many rows Appointments can
contain many services

00:00:30.917 --> 00:00:36.629
and a service can appear in many appointments
Relational databases resolve

00:00:36.655 --> 00:00:42.286
that many-to-many relationship with a junction table
The placement rule is

00:00:42.313 --> 00:00:46.497
worth remembering conceptually in one-to-many put
the foreign key on the many

00:00:46.523 --> 00:00:51.578
side In many-to-many introduce an intersection or
junction table
